1.vh,vw
viewport width =500px
viewport height=600px

then,
    100vw=full viewport width=>500px
    1vw=5px
    50vw=250px
if, 100vw=800px
then,
    1vw=8px
    50vw=400px

similar for height also
if, 100vh=600px
   then, 
       1vh=6px
       50vh=300px

default fontsize is 16px like html,section,main

2.rem=  depends on root element
        default font size is 16px, so we can use that as a base for our calculations
        So,font-size: 2rem;/* Default 1rem is equal to 16px so, (16px * 2)=32px


3.em=   nerest ancestor
        html {
    /* default font size is 16px, so we can use that as a base for our calculations */
    /*2nd nerest ancestor  */
    font-size: 40px;
}
       section {
    font-size: 50px;
    /* 1st nearest ancestor with a font-size of 50px */
}
section h1 {
    /* 3 times the root font size (40px) = 120px */
    /*font-size: 3rem;  2nd nerest ancestor  */
    
    
    /* 1 nearest ancestor with a font-size of 50px, so 3 times 50px = 150px */
    font-size: 3em;

}


clamp: used to give upper limit and lower limit for the view port
example: 
html{
    /* 100vw=1900px*/
    /* 1vw=19px */
    font-size:clamp(14px,1vw,18px);
}